hermes v2026.9.14 (0.21.3): the dashboard's self-hosted OIDC provider
admits every identity the issuer vouches for. Nothing in hermes checks
group membership (plugins/dashboard_auth/self_hosted: the `groups` claim
only becomes Session.org_id, a display string; still so on origin/main,
NousResearch/hermes-agent#55648), so the issuer's own per-client
restriction is the only authorization. An issuer without one (dex) lets
every account it knows into every agent's dashboard.

Fix: `allowed_groups` (HERMES_DASHBOARD_OIDC_ALLOWED_GROUPS, or
dashboard.oauth.self_hosted.allowed_groups; comma list). When set, the
verified ID token's `groups` claim must name one of them. The check sits
in _verify_id_token, which every path that makes a Session goes
through: the login callback (400, no session cookie), each refresh
(RefreshExpiredError: the session ends) and the per-request
re-verification of the stored ID token (None: refresh, then re-login).
The issuer emits `groups` only for the `groups` scope, so the deployment
asks for it. Unset, nothing changes.

